    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "START HERE - MiniMax H3 Ref2VA still image",
      "pos": [
        -900,
        620
      ],
      "size": [
        780,
        670
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "H3 Portrait Lite 1.5 - SINGLE IMAGE USING MINIMAX H3 REF2VA\n1. This is NOT a separate image model. It uses the same Lite MiniMax H3 Ref2VA model/encoder/VAEs as the video workflows.\n2. Upload multiple subject references. Typical swap: Image 1 Face only; Image 2 Identity or Body/proportions; Image 3 Pose/camera only or Scene/environment only.\n3. Keep Still safe swap (pose/scene text-only) for identity swaps. Ollama analyzes every upload, but pose/camera, expression and scene-guide pixels are withheld from H3 and translated into prompt guidance so the guide person's identity does not compete with your subject.\n4. All images visual (comparison) is available when you intentionally want H3 to see the guide pixels directly. It can strengthen composition, but can also pull appearance from that guide.\n5. Start Draft only and review the routing and final H3 prompt. Then change only mode to Generate image.\n6. H3 natively renders its minimum five-frame packet. The workflow decodes all frames, selects one stable/sharp frame, and SaveImage writes ONLY that single result.\n7. High-res (~2 MP, experimental) is the shipped default for this high-resolution still workflow and asks H3 itself to render a larger canvas; it is not an interpolated upscale and may require more VRAM. If it OOMs or looks unstable, switch to Native detail (~1 MP). Preview is about 0.5 MP.\n8. High fidelity = 20 steps + maximum reference size. Standard = 16 steps. Fast preview = 12 steps. Sampler res_multistep, scheduler simple.\n9. Match guide/primary prefers an assigned pose/scene guide for aspect ratio, otherwise the first visual subject ref. Fixed 9:16, 2:3, 4:5, 1:1 and 16:9 are available.\n10. Compatible full-H3 LoRAs can be selected exactly as in the automatic video workflow. No additional large model download is required for this still workflow."
      ]
    }
